atlas provider
# Harvested run6/run7 provider topology. ProviderStateFold already folds provider
# events; these are the resolution/placement/parity graphs above it, still to build.

architecture provider-graph
  canonical_name ProviderGraph
  family provider
  domain Provider / Resolution
  layer provider
  semantic_question Which providers can realize this capability, at what multidimensional metric?
  purpose Capability bids, tournament, fallback tree -- native/frappe/replicated/signal/sidecar/external/commercial/capacity/model/device/human bids scored on a vector (cost/quality/latency/trust/authority/locality/semantic-loss/availability), no scalar collapse. Anycast over equivalent realizations.
  maturity architectural
  node_types CapabilityBid
  node_types ProviderTournament
  edge_types realizes
  edge_types falls_back_to
  forbidden_inference available -> authorized
  forbidden_inference cheapest -> valid
  interacts provider-state
  interacts address-plane
  source_lineage run6/run7 provider topology
  known_gap not built; ProviderStateFold folds events, the route-set daemon advertises/withdraws routes

architecture placement-graph
  canonical_name PlacementGraph
  family provider
  domain Provider / Placement
  layer provider
  semantic_question Where does this run or reside, given locality and resource constraints?
  purpose The material placement of a selected realization across Mac fabric, LAN, GPU, device, remote. Distinct from ProviderGraph (who can) and RuntimeMesh (what instances exist).
  maturity architectural
  node_types PlacementNode
  edge_types placed_on
  forbidden_inference placeable -> authorized to execute there
  interacts address-plane
  source_lineage run6/run7 provider topology
  known_gap not built; CID prefix routing gives placement partitions over content digests

architecture runtime-parity-graph
  canonical_name RuntimeParityGraph
  family provider
  domain Provider / Parity
  layer provider
  semantic_question Do direct, MCP, and HTTP carriers produce the same semantic result?
  purpose Proven semantic equivalence across execution carriers, so route selection can treat them as an equal-cost multipath group.
  maturity architectural
  node_types Carrier
  edge_types parity_with
  forbidden_inference a carrier ran -> semantic parity with the others
  interacts transport-phenotype
  source_lineage run6/run7 provider topology
  known_gap not built; TransportPhenotype proved identical digest across direct/MCP already
